    "created_at": "2018-03-02T09:20:39Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-03-02T09:21:21Z",
    "body": "That is correct.\r\n\r\nHere's an example, if I specify `<input>` it would use the missing value default for the `type` attribute, which is `text`. If I specify `<input type=not-a-value>`, `not-a-value` is invalid, so it would use the invalid value default, but that's not defined, so the missing value default takes effect and makes it treated as `text`.\r\n\r\nInstead of having that, we'd change this to say that both the invalid value default and missing value default are `text`.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
