    "created_at": "2018-03-02T23:42:52Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-03-02T23:42:52Z",
    "body": "That makes a lot more sense, thanks.\r\n\r\nIs there a valid reason why the missing value default and invalid value default can be different? I assume that most of the time when given an invalid value, the element will just behave like it normally does, as if that value was never there (i.e. uses a universal default value).\r\n\r\nFor example, why does [`formenctype`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLFormElement/enctype) specify that there is no missing value default?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
